            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Dymatize ISO100 or Premier Protein better for lactose intolerance?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Dymatize ISO100 is the better choice, since its protein is hydrolyzed whey isolate and whey isolate only, which are filtered to remove most lactose. Premier's blend includes whey concentrate, which carries more lactose, and its label does not give an amount. People with severe intolerance or a milk allergy should avoid both and look at plant protein.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is a Premier Protein shake better than Dymatize ISO100?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Only for convenience. Per Premier's website, the Classic shake gives 30 g of protein and 160 calories with 1 g of sugar, ready to drink. ISO100 is a powder with 25 g per scoop, certified per retailer listings and lower in lactose. In our November checks the shake cost about $1.86 per 25 g on Amazon, against about $2.77 for ISO100 at Vitacost.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Which is better for weight loss, Dymatize or Premier Protein?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  They are nearly tied on calories: ISO100 gives 25 g of protein for 120 calories and Premier 30 g for 150, which is about 125 calories per 25 g. Both have 1 g of sugar. Pick Premier if cost keeps you consistent, or ISO100 if whey concentrate bloats you. Total daily calories matter far more than the powder you choose.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

          </div>
