          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most buyers, Premier Protein powder is the better deal: it gives 30 g of protein per serving at about $1.47 per 25 g in our data, roughly half what ISO100 cost at the retailer price we recorded, and it is soy-free. If you are not drug-tested and whey concentrate does not bother you, there is little reason to pay more.
